-- title:
--   Local structure of the stalk at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, and $M'\neq 0$ divisible by neither. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\xi$, such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K\subseteq L((T))$ be the intermediate field generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ at level $(q\ell)^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, algebraically closed residue field, $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, uniformiser $\varpi$, and compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$; let $j\in K$, $j\neq0$, have Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $j(q)$. Write $\mathfrak X$ for the two-chart integral model over $A$ attached to $j$, obtained as the pushout of the two charts, and $C$ for the chart algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $z\in\mathfrak X$ be such that the germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O=\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$, and let $y\in\operatorname{Spec} C$ map to $z$ under the chart immersion, with the property that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel exactly $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in the set of those $a\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Then: $\mathcal O$ is Noetherian; every $r\in\mathcal O$ agrees modulo $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ with the germ of some element of $A$; for every $r\in\mathcal O$ and every $n$ there is $c\in C$ with $r-\operatorname{germ}_y(c)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^n$; and for $c\in C$, $\operatorname{germ}_y(c)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ if and only if $c\in y$.
--
--   This records the local algebra of the integral model of the modular curve at a supersingular point of the fibre over the closed point of $A$: the stalk is Noetherian, its residue field is generated by the residues of $A$, the chart algebra is dense for the $\mathfrak m$-adic filtration, and the maximal ideal of the stalk pulls back to the prime $y$. It feeds the subsequent analysis of the Drinfeld chart and of the inertia action at such a point.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_isNoetherianRing_stalk_and_residue_and_dense_and_mem_iff_of_mem_ssJSet_of_exists_ringHom.lean

